#             under the author entry once it exists.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, cite it using the metadata below, and always
  cite the source paper of every dataset you use (each data card carries
  its publications with BibTeX).
type: software
title: "MoveAtlas: the open atlas of movement data, human and animal"
abstract: >-
  One Python API (moveatlas) over the movement-disorders corpus: a
  taxonomy-driven registry of catalogued datasets with four enforced
  access cases, canonical contracts per modality family (pose, IMU, EMG,
  force, silhouette, EEG), and patient-level evaluation splits.
authors:
  - family-names: Vasques
    given-names: Xavier
version: 0.1.0.dev0
date-released: "2026-09-08"
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/xaviervasques/moveatlas"
keywords:
  - movement disorders
  - human movement
  - motion capture
  - inertial sensors
  - electromyography
  - electroencephalography
  - foundation models
  - open data
references:
  - type: dataset
    title: "CODY: clinical dystonia video-derived motion dataset (MoveAtlas)"
    authors:
      - family-names: Vasques
        given-names: Xavier
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22232609
    year: 2026
    license: CC-BY-4.0
    notes: >-
      Concept DOI of the CODY derived release (keypoints, SAM3 mask time
      series and labels; no raw video), published on Zenodo on 2026-09-01.
